  "result": "I've completed the season-end retrospective for Season 2. Here's what changed and why:\n\n**Strategy Shift**: Revised from calendar-based \"October peak is proven\" to reactive trigger-based (\"water \u226519\u00b0C + fleet \u22650.5 yt/angler = book within 3-5 days\"). Season 2 taught us: I missed the massive late-September peak (doy 256-273, 16.19 yt/angler) waiting for October, then captured only 1 of 2 planned October trips after burning $950 on early failed plays, finishing rank 9 with 4.5455 fish instead of potential 12-15.\n\n**S3 Execution**: Rewrote `strategy.py` to implement trigger logic monitoring water temp and fleet rolling 5-day averages; updated `notes.md` with detailed postmortem showing that holding PTO 14+ days ahead locked us out of pivots, pre-committing to calendar windows killed flexibility, and boat selection matters (Ocean Odyssey 5.0 vs Mustang 0.0 same class). New playbook: hold all resources until signal confirms, then book 2-3 day_1_5 trips in 7-10 days at proven boats (\u22650.3 yt/angler recent avg).",
